tical environment  so now we get to the heart of this  presentation and we need to answer the  question what is causing label  inaccuracies for cannabis products the  accuracy of the label claim on a  cannabis product is dependent upon the  amount of error incurred during the  testing process error by definition is  the difference between the true result  and the measured result and we encounter  error that is pre-analytical meaning  error that occurred during sampling we  encounter error while the sample is  being tested and we also encounter error  post analytically or after the results  are generated and there will always be  some degree of error error will never go  away  it can only be minimized when we are  sampling the goal is to provide a sample  to the testing laboratory that  accurately represents the total  production batch we need to consider the  physical form of the sample if the  sample is a solid that material may need  to be ground or if it's a liquid that  may need to be homogenized  we need to think about the quantity of  the sample so that the the sample needs  to be statistically representative of  the overall batch or the large-scale  batch we also need to think about the  timing and frequency that the sample is  pulled typically critical batches are  tested or at any point in which the  sample will be sold directly to the  consumer or the batch will be sold to  the consumer  we need to collect samples and have them  tested it is very important to have a  written sampling procedure this  procedure needs to to inform the sampler  on when how and where that sample will  be pulled it needs to give instructions  on the storage and transport of the  sample what kind of analysis required  what happens to the results would the  acceptance criteria are for the results  and also what happens to the retention  samples the sample needs to be tested  for some reason we may need access to it  on the sample itself the name of the  sample the time the person 